ewline \u2014 keep on one line. Good.\n\nThe lesson regex: `window\\.lesson\\s*=\\s*({.+?})\\s*;` \u2014 `{.+?}` non-greedy to first `}` followed by `\\s*;`. JSON `{\"lesson_name\": \"My Lesson\", ...}` \u2014 inner objects? None (flat dict). The first `}` is the closing brace. Good. But careful: if the JSON contains nested objects, non-greedy would stop early. Flat dict is fine.\n\nThen:\n\n```python\nresult = ie._real_extract(url)\nassert result['id'] == '3-7'\nassert result['formats'] == [{'format_id': 'hls-test', 'url': 'https://example.com/hls/lesson7.m3u8', 'ext': 'mp4', 'protocol': 'm3u8_native', 'm3u8_id': 'hls'}]\nassert result['title'] == 'My Lesson'\nassert result['description'] == 'Lesson MD desc'\nassert result['timestamp'] == unified_timestamp('2019-06-01')\nassert result['duration'] == 600\n```\n\nparse_duration('10 minutes') = 600. Good.\n\nAlso assert `_sort_formats` was called (fake_sort.called). And that `_download_webpage` got the right url/video_id: downloaded['url'] == url, downloaded['video_id'] == '3-7'.\n\nTest 3: no lesson \u2192 title fallback via '>Lecture:'.\n\n```python\nwebpage = \"player.playlist = [{'file': 'https://example.com/hls/x.m3u8'}]; <h1>Lecture: Fallback Title</h1>\"\n```\n\nWait, the regex `>Lecture\\s*:\\s*(?P<value>[^<]+)` \u2014 needs `>Lecture:` literally. So webpage must contain `>Lecture: Fallback Title`. E.g. `<div>Lecture: Fallback Title</div>` \u2014 the `>` before Lecture: `<div>Lecture:` \u2192 `>Lecture: Fallback Title` matches with value ' Fallback Title'? `\\s*` after colon consumes leading spaces; `[^<]+` captures 'Fallback Title'. Good.\n\nThen result['title'] == 'Fallback Title'. And lesson absent \u2192 no title/description/timestamp/duration from lesson. Assert 'title' == 'Fallback Title', and description/timestamp/duration not in result (info only has id and formats plus title).\n\nTest 4: no lesson, title via `lessonName = 'Another Title'`:\n\n```python\nwebpage = \"player.playlist = [...]; var lessonName = 'Another Title';\"\n```\n\nRegex: `lessonName\\s*=\\s*([\"\\'])(?P<value>(?:(?!\\1).)+)\\1` \u2014 matches `lessonName = 'Another Title'` \u2192 value 'Another Title'. Good.\n\nHmm, but wait: in test 3 and 4, `_search_regex` for lesson returns default '{}' \u2192 `_parse_json('{}', ...)` \u2192 {} \u2192 falsy. Good.\n\nAlso, should I test `_parse_json` failure path (invalid lesson JSON with fatal=False \u2192 None)? That covers `fatal=False` behavior but it's in common.py, not our lines. The `if lesson:` False branch is covered by tests 3/4. Fine.\n\nNow \u2014 do I need to worry about `mobj.group('chapter_id', 'lesson_id', 'course_id')`? `match.group(*names)` with multiple names returns tuple. Fine.\n\nNow, the exact _VALID_URL \u2014 let me fetch. Also fetch InfoExtractor methods to confirm signatures for the fakes.\n\nAlso \u2014 one more consideration: `ie._real_extract(url)` calls `re.match(self._VALID_URL, url)`. If URL doesn't match, mobj is None \u2192 AttributeError. So URLs must match. Get _VALID_URL first.\n\nLet me also think about whether `LinuxAcademyIE` has `_WORKING` or geo-bypass stuff that runs in `_real_extract` \u2014 no.\n\nPotential issue: `InfoExtractor.__init__` might require downloader for `_download_webpage` \u2014 patched, fine.\n\nAnother potential issue: `_parse_json` in newer youtube-dl versions calls `transform_source` and also `self._search_regex`? No.\n\nOK, let me also double check `clean_html` behavior: `clean_html('<b>Course description</b>')` \u2192 'Course description'. Yes.\n\n`clean_html('<i>Desc B</i>')` \u2192 'Desc B'. `clean_html('<p>Text C</p>')` \u2192 'Text C'. Good.\n\nNow about `urljoin(url, item.get('url'))` where url is the course page URL. If course URL ends with '/course/dashboard/my-course', urljoin(base, '/lesson/a') \u2192 scheme+host + '/lesson/a'. Good.\n\nBut wait \u2014 what if _VALID_URL's course_id group is something like `course/dashboard/(?P<course_id>[^/?#&]+)`? Then URL 'https://app.linuxacademy.com/course/dashboard/my-course' matches with course_id='my-course'. \n\nAlternatively the real _VALID_URL might be:\n\n```python\n_VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n    https?://\n        (?:\n            linuxacademy\\.com/|\n            (?:www\\.)?app\\.linuxacademy\\.com/\n        )\n    (?:\n        course/dashboard/(?P<course_id>[^/?#&]+)|\n        chapter/(?P<chapter_id>[^/?#&]+)/lesson/(?P<lesson_id>[^/?#&]+)\n    )\n'''\n```\n\nLet me just call get_info.\n\nActually, I realize I should also check `InfoExtractor.ie_key` to assert correctly. `LinuxAcademyIE.ie_key()` \u2192 'LinuxAcademy'. I'll assert `entry['ie_key'] == LinuxAcademyIE.ie_key()` \u2014 self-consistent.\n\nLet me make the get_info calls now:\n\n1. `LinuxAcademyIE._VALID_URL`\n2. `InfoExtractor._search_regex`\n3. `InfoExtractor._parse_json`\n4. `InfoExtractor._extract_m3u8_formats`\n5. `InfoExtractor._sort_formats`\n6. `InfoExtractor._download_webpage`\n7. `unified_timestamp`\n8. `parse_duration`\n9. `urljoin`\n10. `clean_html`\n11. `InfoExtractor.ie_key`\n\nThese are all independent \u2014 batch them.\n\nThen write the final test file.\n\nLet me draft the full test file now (to be refined after get_info):\n\n```python\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport json\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.extractor.linuxacademy import LinuxAcademyIE\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import parse_duration, unified_timestamp, urljoin\n\n\ndef _install_fake_io(monkeypatch, webpage):\n    \"\"\"Patch network-facing helpers of LinuxAcademyIE with fakes.\"\"\"\n    calls = {'download': [], 'm3u8': [], 'sorted': False}\n\n    def fake_download_webpage(self, url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        calls['download'].append((url, video_id))\n        return webpage\n\n    def fake_extract_m3u8_formats(self, m3u8_url, video_id, ext=None, **kwargs):\n        calls['m3u8'].append((m3u8_url, video_id, ext, kwargs))\n        return [{\n            'format_id': '%s-test' % kwargs.get('m3u8_id'),\n            'url': m3u8_url,\n            'ext': ext,\n            'protocol': kwargs.get('entry_protocol'),\n        }]\n\n    def fake_sort_formats(self, formats=None, field_preference=None):\n        calls['sorted'] = True\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(LinuxAcademyIE, '_download_webpage', fake_download_webpage)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(LinuxAcademyIE, '_extract_m3u8_formats', fake_extract_m3u8_formats)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(LinuxAcademyIE, '_sort_formats', fake_sort_formats)\n    return calls\n\n\ndef test_course_playlist(monkeypatch):\n    course_id = 'linux-academy-weekly-news'\n    url = 'https://app.linuxacademy.com/course/dashboard/%s' % course_id\n    module = {\n        'title': 'Test Course',\n        'md_desc': '<b>Course description</b>',\n        'duration': '1 hour',\n        'items': [\n            'not-a-dict',\n            {'type': {'name': 'Section', 'slug': 'section'},\n             'course_name': 'Chapter One', 'course_module': 'module-1'},\n            {'type': {'name': 'Quiz', 'slug': 'quiz'}},\n            {'type': {'name': 'Lesson', 'slug': 'lesson'},\n             'lesson_name': 'Lesson A', 'url': '/lesson/a',\n             'date': '2019-01-01', 'duration': '5 minutes',\n             'md_desc': 'MD desc A'},\n            {'type': {'name': 'Section', 'slug': 'section'},\n             'course_name': 'Chapter Two', 'course_module': 'module-2'},\n            {'type': {'name': 'lesson', 'slug': 'lesson'},\n             'title': 'Lesson B', 'url': 'https://example.com/lesson/b',\n             'created_on': '2019-01-02', 'duration': '6:00',\n             'description': '<i>Desc B</i>'},\n            {'type': {'name': 'lesson', 'slug': 'lesson'},\n             'title': 'Lesson C', 'url': '/lesson/c',\n             'text': '<p>Text C</p>'},\n            {'type': {'name': 'lesson', 'slug': 'lesson'},\n             'title': 'Lesson D'},  # no url -> skipped\n        ],\n    }\n    webpage = '<html><script>window.module = %s;</script></html>' % json.dumps(module)\n    calls = _install_fake_io(monkeypatch, webpage)\n\n    ie = LinuxAcademyIE()\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n\n    # webpage was fetched with the expected args\n    assert calls['download'] == [(url, course_id)]\n\n    assert result['_type'] == 'playlist'\n    assert result['id'] == course_id\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Course'\n    assert result['description'] == 'Course description'\n    assert result['duration'] == 3600\n\n    entries = result['entries']\n    assert len(entries) == 3  # non-dict, quiz and url-less lesson are skipped\n\n    a, b, c = entries\n    assert a['_type'] == 'url_transparent'\n    assert a['ie_key'] == LinuxAcademyIE.ie_key()\n    assert a['url'] == urljoin(url, '/lesson/a')\n    assert a['title'] == 'Lesson A'\n    assert a['description'] == 'MD desc A'\n    assert a['timestamp'] == unified_timestamp('2019-01-01')\n    assert a['duration'] == 300\n    assert a['chapter'] == 'Chapter One'\n    assert a['chapter_id'] == 'module-1'\n    assert a['chapter_number'] == 1\n\n    assert b['url'] == 'https://example.com/lesson/b'\n    assert b['title'] == 'Lesson B'\n    assert b['description'] == 'Desc B'\n    assert b['timestamp'] == unified_timestamp('2019-01-02')\n    assert b['duration'] == 360\n    assert b['chapter'] == 'Chapter Two'\n    assert b['chapter_id'] == 'module-2'\n    assert b['chapter_number'] == 2\n\n    assert c['url'] == urljoin(url, '/lesson/c')\n    assert c['title'] == 'Lesson C'\n    assert c['description'] == 'Text C'\n    assert c['timestamp'] is None\n    assert c['duration'] is None\n    assert c['chapter'] == 'Chapter Two'\n    assert c['chapter_number'] == 2\n```\n\nWait \u2014 entry D has no url \u2192 skipped. But hold on: entry D has 'title' but no url \u2192 `lesson_url = urljoin(url, None)` \u2192 None \u2192 continue. Good, covers line 188-189.\n\nHmm, but wait: does `urljoin(base, None)` return None? youtube-dl's urljoin:\n\n```python\ndef urljoin(base, path):\n    if isinstance(base, bytes):\n        ...\n    if not isinstance(path, compat_str):\n        return None\n    if not isinstance(base, compat_str):\n        return None\n    return urllib.parse.urljoin(base, path)\n```\n\nSomething like that. Yes, returns None for non-str path. Good.\n\nNow single video tests:\n\n```python\ndef test_single_video_with_lesson(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://app.linuxacademy.com/chapter/3/lesson/7'\n    m3u8_url = 'https://example.com/hls/lesson7.m3u8'\n    playlist = json.dumps([{'file': m3u8_url}])\n    lesson = json.dumps({\n        'lesson_name': 'My Lesson',\n        'md_desc': 'Lesson MD desc',\n        'date': '2019-06-01',\n        'duration': '10 minutes',\n    })\n    webpage = 'player.playlist = %s; window.lesson = %s;' % (playlist, lesson)\n    calls = _install_fake_io(monkeypatch, webpage)\n\n    ie = LinuxAcademyIE()\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n\n    assert calls['download'] == [(url, '3-7')]\n    assert calls['m3u8'] == [(m3u8_url, '3-7', 'mp4', {'entry_protocol': 'm3u8_native', 'm3u8_id': 'hls'})]\n    assert calls['sorted'] is True\n\n    assert result['id'] == '3-7'\n    assert result['formats'] == [{'format_id': 'hls-test', 'url': m3u8_url, 'ext': 'mp4', 'protocol': 'm3u8_native'}]\n    assert result['title'] == 'My Lesson'\n    assert result['description'] == 'Lesson MD desc'\n    assert result['timestamp'] == unified_timestamp('2019-06-01')\n    assert result['duration'] == 600\n```\n\nHmm, careful with the m3u8 call kwargs assertion \u2014 `_real_extract` calls:\n\n```python\nself._extract_m3u8_formats(\n    m3u8_url, item_id, 'mp4', entry_protocol='m3u8_native',\n    m3u8_id='hls')\n```\n\nSo kwargs = {'entry_protocol': 'm3u8_native', 'm3u8_id': 'hls'}. My fake signature: `def fake_extract_m3u8_formats(self, m3u8_url, video_id, ext=None, **kwargs)`. Called with positional (m3u8_url, item_id, 'mp4') and kwargs. Good.\n\nBut asserting exact kwargs dict equality is brittle if the real code passes more kwargs \u2014 it doesn't. OK.\n\nActually, maybe simpler: just record m3u8_url and assert formats content. I'll keep the call record but assert loosely:\n\n```python\nassert len(calls['m3u8']) == 1\nm3u8_call = calls['m3u8'][0]\nassert m3u8_call[0] == m3u8_url\nassert m3u8_call[1] == '3-7'\nassert m3u8_call[2] == 'mp4'\nassert m3u8_call[3]['entry_protocol'] == 'm3u8_native'\nassert m3u8_call[3]['m3u8_id'] == 'hls'\n```\n\nTest 3: fallback title via Lecture regex:\n\n```python\ndef test_single_video_title_fallback_lecture(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://app.linuxacademy.com/chapter/1/lesson/2'\n    webpage = (\n        \"player.playlist = \" + json.dumps([{'file': 'https://example.com/hls/a.m3u8'}]) + \";\"\n        \"<h1>Lecture: Fallback Title</h1>\"\n    )\n    calls = _install_fake_io(monkeypatch, webpage)\n    ie = LinuxAcademyIE()\n    result = ie._real_extract(url)\n    assert result['id'] == '1-2'\n    assert result['title'] == 'Fallback Title'\n    assert 'description' not in result\n    assert 'timestamp' not in result\n    assert 'duration' not in result\n    assert len(result['formats']) == 1\n```\n\nWait \u2014 the playlist regex: `player\\.playlist\\s*=\\s*(\\[.+?\\])\\s*;`. The webpage: `player.playlist = [{\"file\": \"https://example.com/hls/a.m3u8\"}];<h1>Lecture: Fallback Title</h1>`. The regex `\\[.+?\\]` non-greedy: matches `[{\"file\": \"https://example.com/hls/a.m3u8\"}]` \u2014 first `]` is at the end of the array. Good. Then `\\s*;` matches `;`. Good.\n\nHmm wait, there's a subtlety: `.+?` \u2014 the JSON contains `\"` and `/` \u2014 fine. But does it contain `]` earlier? The URL has no `]`. Good.\n\nTest 4: fallback via lessonName regex:\n\n```python\ndef test_single_video_title_fallback_lesson_name(monkeypatch):\n    url = 'https://app.linuxacademy.com/chapter/4/lesson/9'\n    webpage = (\n        \"player.playlist = \" + json.dumps([{'file': 'https://example.com/hls/b.m3u8'}]) + \";\"\n        \"var lessonName = 'Another Fallback';\"\n    )\n    ...\n    assert result['title'] == 'Another Fallback'\n``