lass-level setattr via monkeypatch: as analyzed, for inherited attributes, monkeypatch stores notset and deletes on undo \u2192 clean. For instance-level, it would leave a bound-method instance attribute \u2014 but instance is discarded. I'll use class-level to be safest.\n\nWait, actually let me re-verify the monkeypatch undo logic for class-level setattr where the attribute is inherited:\n\n```python\ndef setattr(self, target, name, value=notset, raising=True):\n    ...\n    oldval = getattr(target, name, notset)\n    if raising and oldval is notset:\n        raise AttributeError(...)\n    # avoid class descriptors like staticmethod/classmethod\n    if inspect.isclass(target):\n        oldval = target.__dict__.get(name, notset)\n    self._setattr.append((target, name, oldval))\n    setattr(target, name, value)\n```\n\nundo:\n\n```python\ndef undo(self):\n    ...\n    for obj, name, value in reversed(self._setattr):\n        if value is not notset:\n            setattr(obj, name, value)\n        else:\n            delattr(obj, name)\n```\n\nSo: oldval = notset (inherited) \u2192 undo does `delattr(LinuxAcademyIE, '_download_webpage')` \u2192 removes the shadowing attribute \u2192 inherited method visible again. Clean. \u2713\n\nAnd `raising=True` check: `oldval = getattr(target, name, notset)` \u2192 found (inherited) \u2192 no raise. \u2713\n\nGreat.\n\nNow, one more consideration: since I patch class attributes, if a test fails mid-way, monkeypatch still undoes (fixture finalizer). \u2713\n\nLet me now also decide: should the fakes be defined inside `_patch_io` and closed over `webpage`? Yes.\n\nEdge: multiple tests each call `_patch_io` with their own webpage \u2014 independent. \u2713\n\nNow, final check on the course webpage: I wrap in `<script>...</script>` \u2014 the regex doesn't care. Keep it simple: `webpage = \"window.module = %s;\" % json.dumps(module)`. But hmm \u2014 `_search_regex` searches the whole webpage; fine.\n\nActually wait, there's one poten